  "description": "Erection of single storey ground floor rear conservatory&nbsp;",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal, by reason of its size, design and siting, without a detailed assessment to confirm otherwise, has the potential to result in harm to trees in the surrounding area, contrary to policy LP51 (&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Tree Management and Landscaping) of the Hackney Local Plan (2020) and policy G1 (Green infrastructure) of the London Plan (2020). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal, by reason of its size, design, scale and siting, adjacent to a locally listed building, comprises an incongruous form of works resulting in an obtrusive and incompatible form of development which would fail to respect the application property, the wider terrace and would thus fail to preserve or enhance the character and appearance Stoke Newington Conservation Area and would fail to conserve or enhance and reveal the significance of the locally listed building and its setting. As such the proposed development is contrary to policies D3 (Optimising Site Capacity Through the Design-Led Approach), D4 (Delivering good design) and HC1 (Heritage conservation and growth) of the London Plan (2021) and policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character), LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets), LP4 (Non-Designated Heritage Assets) and LP17 (Housing Design) of the Local Plan 2033 (2020)n and the guidance contained within Hackney&#x27;s Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2025).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
